<title>USA: Amarillo feeder cattle not well tested - USDA.</title>
<headline>Amarillo feeder cattle not well tested - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>AMARILLO 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Feeder steers and heifers under 600 lbs not well tested, heavier weights $1.00 per cwt higher, compared to last week, USDA said.</p>
<p>Bulk supply Medium and Large 1-2 400-950 lb feeder steers and 400-850 lb feeder heifers. Trade moderate. Demand good.</p>
<p>Feeder Steers - Medium and Large 1 - 600-700 lbs 79.50- 81.00, lot 602 lbs 85.00; 700-800 lbs 74.25-76.10; 800-815 lbs 73.60- 77.00; 900-950 lbs 69.00-69.75. Medium and Large 1-2 - 600-700 lbs 70.50-77.25; few 700-900 lbs 70.25-72.25.</p>
<p>Feeder Heifers - Medium and Large 1 - 600-700 lbs 71.75-73.00, load 690 lbs fleshy 67.90; 700-800 lbs 73.20-75.00; 800-850 lbs 68.25-69.00. Medium and Large 1-2 - 600-800 lbs 64.50-70.50.</p>
<p>Receipts - 2,400</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
